---
source: crates/wolf_mem/tests/mem_diagnostics.rs
expression: render_mem(src)
---
error[E1010]: `worker` is spawned as a proc and may outlive this frame, and `msg`'s bytes live in region `pass`, which is freed with its scope — while the proc may still be reading them
  --> mem:///main.lu:10:35
   |
 8 |     region pass {
   |            ---- region `pass` is created here and freed with its scope — everything in it is freed wholesale
 9 |         let msg = "built in pass, {n} uses"
   |                   ------------------------- allocated here, into region `pass`
10 |         let c = spawn proc worker(msg, out)
   |                                   ^^^ this argument's bytes are in region `pass`
   |
   = note: a `spawn proc` argument crosses into a domain that outlives the spawner [conc.proc.arg],
     and a `str` crosses as its view: the bytes stay where they were built, so they must
     outlive the frame that spawns [mem.region.escape]. Build the value where it outlives
     this frame — outside the region block — or spawn from a function that is handed the
     value as a parameter and joins the proc before it returns; a literal or a scalar
     argument owns no region storage.
